{"title":"Career Roadmap — Lab Technologist","role":"Lab Technologist","summary":"A Lab Technologist performs laboratory testing, sample preparation, instrument operation, quality control, data analysis, and documentation. With a B.Sc Biochemistry, the student can build a strong foundation for laboratory careers across:","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science - General / Honours)","Course":"Biochemistry"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Lab Technologist performs laboratory testing, sample preparation, instrument operation, quality control, data analysis, and documentation. With a B.Sc Biochemistry, the student can build a strong foundation for laboratory careers across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical diagnostics"},{"text":"Pharmaceutical laboratories"},{"text":"Biotechnology"},{"text":"Food and beverage testing"},{"text":"Research laboratories"},{"text":"Molecular diagnostics"},{"text":"Environmental testing"},{"text":"Biopharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Academic and research institutions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning for a Biochemistry graduate is to combine biochemistry + laboratory techniques + instrumentation + quality systems + data analysis."},{"type":"p","text":"For clinical laboratory roles, exact eligibility, scope of practice, and registration requirements can vary by role, institution, and applicable Indian regulations. Students should verify the current requirements for the specific clinical designation they target."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc Biochemistry"},{"text":"Laboratory fundamentals + instrumentation + practical training"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Lab Trainee / Junior Technologist"},{"text":"Sample processing + routine testing + QC"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"Lab T